{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486833-rebels-anarchs-or-terrorists-in-vtr","id":486833,"title":"Rebels, Anarchs or Terrorists in VtR?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-20T16:46:58-07:00","id":486833,"title":"Rebels, Anarchs or Terrorists in VtR?","content":"I recently started searching for any kind of group or specific person that opposes the Traditions, or is specifically fighting against the Masquerade. I was thinking something similar to a guerilla group. I have checked many supplements but I can't find anything. Does anybody have an idea about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5753-azvos2","name":"azvos2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:58:42-07:00","id":486861,"title":"","content":"Some radical Carthians might be up for that. The Commonwealth from Danse Macabre definitely would be, and might actually have cities where they've successfully integrated mortal and kindred societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:13:16-07:00","id":486872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>azvos2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486833-rebels-anarchs-or-terrorists-in-vtr#post486833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recently started searching for any kind of group or specific person that opposes the Traditions, or is specifically fighting against the Masquerade. I was thinking something similar to a guerilla group. I have checked many supplements but I can't find anything. Does anybody have an idea about that?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Strix! The Brood, in 1e, filled this role as well - they were the hell raisers.<br /> <br /> The tier 3 conspiracy in Dance Macabre had the goal of revealing vamps to humans. They were Carthians taken to gonzo levels. <br /> <br /> Pretty much anyone other than the Invictus and Lance would likely be up for it with some twisting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:46:48-07:00","id":486883,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, the Carthians and their Commonwealth counterparts, the Strix and some aspects of Belial's Brood. I'd like to point out hat the Brood were more than they were depicted in the first edition corebook, at least during first edition. And the Commonwealth aren't exactly terrorists. They're certainly trying to bring down the Masquerade but they're doing it in a very subtle manner and hoping it will lead to a sort of equality. They're city planners.<br /> <br /> Also the VII are probably considered noteworthy terrorists, as they are sort of at war with the rest of vampire kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}